            "name": "Signed Financing Programs Retrieval"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1765979488024"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_BUSINESS_OBJECT_FUNCTION_SIGNED_FINANCING_PROGRAMS_RETRIEVAL",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1765953286609",
          "id": "1765980040944",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1777473337083_1",
              "name": "currentDate",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{}",
          "type": "BO_FUNCTION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.25
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT OSS 120B (Basic)",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Dynamic Discount Program Selector"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1765979976132"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_DYNAMIC_DISCOUNT_PROGRAM_SELECTOR",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1765953286609",
          "id": "1765979488024",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765979488027_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# CONTEXT:\n- input message: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n- chat history: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.chatHistory}}\n- signed financing program list: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_BUSINESS_OBJECT_FUNCTION_SIGNED_FINANCING_PROGRAMS_RETRIEVAL.$output}}\n\n# GUIDELINES:\n- Use both the input message and the chat history as context.\n- Determine whether the user has selected a Dynamic Discount financing program that exists in the signed financing program list.\n- A program is considered selected only if there is an exact name match (case-insensitive comparison allowed) between an entry in the signed financing program list and the Dynamic Discount financing program name requested by the user.\n- Do not assume or infer a program name if there is no exact match.\n- If there is only one Dynamic Discount financing program in the signed financing program list, automatically select it, even if the input message does not contain any information about the Dynamic Discount financing program name.\n\n- If a matching dynamic discount financing program is selected:\n    - Set programSelected = true\n    - Get the matching dynamic discount financing program from the signed financing program list.\n    - Set dynamicDiscountName = its name.\n    - Set dynamicDiscountProgramId = its financingProgramId.\n\n    - Set minimumDiscountRate = the program's minimumDiscountRate.\n    - Set maximumDiscountRate = the program's maximumDiscountRate.\n    - Set defaultDiscountRate = the program's defaultDiscountRate.\n\n    - If the user is requesting a specific discount rate for offer creation, the discount rate/APR may appear in the user’s input or in the benefit analysis “what-if” scenarios from the chat history:\n        - Requested rate extraction (strict):\n            - Set requestedRate = the extracted numeric discount rate (numeric only).\n            - Extract the numeric part only; strip % and ignore adjacent text such as (default), default, previewed, using, percentage, etc.\n            - Example: “12% (default)” → requestedRate = 12.\n            - Do not concatenate numbers. Never build requestedRate by removing characters from the entire message.\n            - Only extract a rate from a single token/substring that:\n                - is immediately followed by % (e.g., 12%, 12.5%), OR\n                - is explicitly labeled discount rate / APR (e.g., “APR 12”, “discount rate: 12”).\n            - If multiple numbers exist in the message (e.g., 12% and week 5), the only valid requestedRate is the one tied to % or labeled APR/discount.\n        - If the user provides a numeric rate even if they call it “default” (e.g., “12% (default)”), treat it as an explicit requestedRate and validate it.\n          Only fall back to defaultDiscountRate when no numeric rate is present in the user message/chat history (in that case requestedRate = null).\n        - Carry-over suppression (out-of-range rate acknowledged):\n            - If the chat history contains an offer preview/response explicitly stating that the requested discount rate is not within the minimum and maximum allowed range (e.g., “not within the minimum and maximum… so the offer will be created using the default discount rate instead”), then:\n                - Do not carry forward any previously requested discount rate from earlier turns.\n                - Only set requestedRate if the current input message contains a new valid rate (per the strict extraction rules).\n                - Otherwise set requestedRate = null, set discountRate = defaultDiscountRate (numeric only), and set isAprWithinAllowedRange = true.\n\n        - Convert minimumDiscountRate, maximumDiscountRate, defaultDiscountRate, and requestedRate to numbers by removing % and any non-numeric characters (except .). Compare using numeric values only.\n\n        - If requestedRate is not null AND (minimumDiscountRate <= requestedRate  AND  requestedRate <= maximumDiscountRate):\n            - Set discountRate = requestedRate (numeric only).\n            - Set isAprWithinAllowedRange = true\n            - Specifically: if requestedRate == minimumDiscountRate OR requestedRate == maximumDiscountRate, it is within range.\n        - Else:\n            - Set discountRate = defaultDiscountRate (numeric only).\n            - Set isAprWithinAllowedRange = false\n\n    - Else (no requested rate found):\n        - Set requestedRate = null\n        - Set discountRate = defaultDiscountRate (numeric only).\n        - Set isAprWithinAllowedRange = true\n\n- Otherwise:\n    - Set programSelected = false\n\n- Output only the value of:\n  programSelected, dynamicDiscountName, dynamicDiscountProgramId,\n  requestedRate, minimumDiscountRate, maximumDiscountRate, defaultDiscountRate,\n  isAprWithinAllowedRange, discountRate.\n  Do not include any extra text or explanation."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"programSelected\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        \"dynamicDiscountName\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"dynamicDiscountProgramId\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"discountRate\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n        },\n        \"isAprWithinAllowedRange\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        \"requestedRate\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n        },\n        \"minimumDiscountRate\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n        },\n        \"maximumDiscountRate\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n        },\n        \"defaultDiscountRate\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Check Financing Program Selected"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1766491420643",
            "false": "1765981079958"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_IF_CONDITION_CHECK_FINANCING_PROGRAM_SELECTED",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1767784385554",
          "id": "1765979976132",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765979976133_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_DYNAMIC_DISCOUNT_PROGRAM_SELECTOR.$output.programSelected}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.25
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT OSS 120B (Basic)",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Draft Offer Creation Approval Checker"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1766508191349"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_DRAFT_OFFER_CREATION_APPROVAL_CHECKER",
          "id": "1766491420643",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1766491420645_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# CONTEXT\n- input message: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n- chat history: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.chatHistory}}\n\n# TASK\n- Decide whether to proceed with offer creation based ONLY on whether a valid draft offer preview was already shown and whether the user has approved it without requesting changes.\n\n# DEFINITIONS\n- A “valid draft offer preview” is a message from the agent that clearly indicates it is a DRAFT offer preview (not just analysis) and includes ALL fields:\n  - Supplier\n  - Due In\n  - Program\n  - Program Type\n  - Discount Rate\n\n- Allowed post-preview change fields (ONLY these count as changes):\n  - Supplier\n  - Financing Program (Program and/or Program Type)\n  - Discount Rate (APR)\n\n- Non-allowed fields rule (critical):\n  - Ignore ALL fields not listed in “Allowed post-preview change fields” when deciding approval vs. change.\n  - Mentions of Business Unit, currency, Due In/week, installment weeks, payment terms, amounts, invoice numbers, etc. must NEVER trigger a change and must NOT be required to match the preview.\n\n- Normalization rules (for comparisons):\n  - Compare strings case-insensitively.\n  - Ignore extra punctuation/parentheses.\n  - Program and Program Type must be compared as separate fields (do NOT compare a combined phrase to a single field).\n\n- **Hard scoping rule (critical):**\n  - When analyzing what the “user requested”, ONLY use `currentUserMessage` (defined in Step 0).\n  - NEVER treat text in this instruction prompt (including examples like “30%”) as user content.\n\n## STEP 0 — DEFINE THE CURRENT USER MESSAGE (CRITICAL)\n- Define `currentUserMessage` using ONLY `{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}` as input.\n\n## STEP 1 — FIND THE LAST VALID DRAFT PREVIEW\n- From chat history, locate the MOST RECENT agent message that qualifies as a valid draft offer preview.\n- Qualification rule (robust to HTML tables):\n  - It contains the phrase “Draft Offer Preview” (case-insensitive), AND\n  - It contains ALL five field labels somewhere in the message text:\n    - Supplier, Due In, Program, Program Type, Discount Rate\n- If no qualifying preview exists: proceedWithOfferCreation = false.\n\n- Extract from that preview:\n  - previewSuppliers (list)\n  - previewProgram (string)\n  - previewProgramType (string)\n  - previewDiscountRateNumeric (numeric only; e.g., “12%” → 12)\n    - Extract ONLY from the Discount Rate field/cell in the draft offer preview.\n  - previewIndicatesDefaultWillBeUsed (boolean):\n    - true if the preview text explicitly says the offer “will be created using the default discount rate instead” (or equivalent).\n\n## STEP 2 — DETECT USER INTENT (USE currentUserMessage ONLY)\n- Approval intent includes phrases like: “create”, “proceed”, “go ahead”, “submit”, “yes”, “approved”, “looks good”.\n- Negative intent overrides approval intent:\n  - If the user expresses “don’t / do not”, “stop”, “cancel”, “hold”, “not yet”, “wait” → proceedWithOfferCreation = false.\n- If no approval/proceed intent: proceedWithOfferCreation = false.\n\n- Explicit approval-by-reference:\n  - If the user says proceed/create AND references the current/above/shown preview (e.g., “use the preview above”),\n    treat as approval UNLESS Step 3 finds a change.\n\n- Explicit approval-by-restating matching allowed fields:\n  - If the user expresses approval/proceed intent AND states allowed-field values that match the preview, treat as approval even without referencing “preview”.\n\n## STEP 3 — DETECT POST-PREVIEW CHANGES (ONLY ALLOWED FIELDS; USE currentUserMessage ONLY)\n- Scope rule (critical):\n  - Detect post-preview changes based ONLY on values explicitly present in `currentUserMessage`.\n  - Do NOT use older user turns in chat history to infer an “active” change request.\n\n### 3A — Supplier change detection\n- If `currentUserMessage` mentions suppliers:\n  - If any mentioned supplier is NOT in previewSuppliers → change.\n  - If mentioned suppliers are a subset of previewSuppliers → NOT a change.\n\n### 3B — Program / Program Type change detection\n- Compare ONLY against `currentUserMessage`:\n  - If it provides a different program/program type than preview → change.\n\n### 3C — Discount Rate change detection (INTENT-GATED; CURRENT-MESSAGE ONLY)\n- IMPORTANT: A percent number in the message is NOT automatically a requested new rate.\n- IMPORTANT: Do not consider previous rate change requests from chat history.\n- userRequestsRateChange = true ONLY if `currentUserMessage` uses explicit change/set language tied to rate/APR/discount.\n\n- userWantsDefaultRate = true if `currentUserMessage` says “use default discount rate”, “program’s default discount rate”, “use the default”, “default rate”.\n\n- If userWantsDefaultRate = true AND userRequestsRateChange = false:\n  - If `currentUserMessage` says proceed/create AND indicates default that equals previewDiscountRateNumeric,\n    then this is explicit approval and NOT a rate change (ignore any prior request).\n\n- If userRequestsRateChange = true, extract NEW rate from `currentUserMessage` ONLY:\n  - Consider only candidates that include “%” OR are within 3 words of “discount”, “APR”, “rate”, or “percent”.\n  - Ignore unrelated numbers.\n  - If NEW != previewDiscountRateNumeric → change.\n\n## STEP 4 — FINAL DECISION\n- If no valid draft preview → false\n- Else if negative intent → false\n- Else if approval intent present in `currentUserMessage` AND no allowed-field changes detected in `currentUserMessage` → true\n- Else → false\n\n# OUTPUT\n- Output ONLY: proceedWithOfferCreation\n- If proceedWithOfferCreation is false also output: reason"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"proceedWithOfferCreation\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        }\n        \"reason\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Create Group By Filter",
            "returnType": "array",
            "sourceCode": "let paymentBenefitRes = $context.$triggers.REST.$input.payablesBalance;\n\nlet result = [];\n\nif (!Array.isArray(paymentBenefitRes)) {\n    paymentBenefitRes = paymentBenefitRes ? [paymentBenefitRes] : [];\n}\n\nfor (const benefit of paymentBenefitRes) {\n    result.push({\n        supplierName: benefit.supplierTypeHierarchy.supplierName,\n        sevenDayBucket: benefit.daysRemainingSevenDayBucketHierarchy.sevenDayBucket,\n        invoiceRemainingAmount: benefit.invoiceRemainingAmount\n    });\n}\nreturn result;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771654220283"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_CODE_CREATE_GROUP_BY_FILTER",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1766491608645",
          "id": "1766508191349",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Proceed With Offer Creation"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1772006126716",
            "false": "1766491754437"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_IF_CONDITION_PROCEED_WITH_OFFER_CREATION",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1767784385554",
          "id": "1766491608645",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1766491608646_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_DRAFT_OFFER_CREATION_APPROVAL_CHECKER.$output.proceedWithOfferCreation}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
