              "value": "{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.endDay}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1773258097226_7",
              "name": "groupByFilter",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_CODE_REMOVE_INVOICEREMAININGAMOUNT_FROM_GROUP_BY_FILTER.$output.result}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{}",
          "type": "BO_FUNCTION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.25
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT OSS 120B (Basic)",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Draft Offer Creation Status Messenger"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1767784552260"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_DRAFT_OFFER_CREATION_STATUS_MESSENGER",
          "id": "1766512987308",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1766512987309_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# GUIDELINES\n\n- Retrieve the draft offer creation status from {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_BUSINESS_OBJECT_FUNCTION_CREATE_DRAFT_OFFER.$output}}.\n- Inform the user of the draft offer creation status, clearly indicating whether the draft offer was created successfully or if there was an issue.\n- If draft offer generation is successful:\n    - Use offerSummaryList from the result. It is an array of objects containing vendorName, installmentCount, and installmentAmtSum : [{vendorName: '', installmentCount: '', installmentAmtSum: ''}, ...].\n    - Aggregate offerSummaryList by vendorName before generating the table.\n    - Treat installmentCount and installmentAmtSum as numeric values when summing; treat missing or null values as 0.\n    - Return exactly one row per unique supplier, even when multiple offer records exist for the same supplier because of different supplier sites.\n    - Do not display supplier-site details, offer IDs, or separate site-level rows.\n    - For each supplier:\n        - Supplier = vendorName.\n        - Installment Count = the sum of installmentCount across all offerSummaryList records for that supplier.\n        - Outstanding Balance = the sum of installmentAmtSum across all offerSummaryList records for that supplier. Add currency code \"{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.currencyCode}}\".\n        - Program = {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_DYNAMIC_DISCOUNT_PROGRAM_SELECTOR.$output.dynamicDiscountName}}.\n        - Program Type = \"Dynamic Discounting\".\n        - Discount Rate = {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_DYNAMIC_DISCOUNT_PROGRAM_SELECTOR.$output.discountRate}}. Display only the numeric value with a % suffix.\n    - Generate a table containing the aggregated supplier-level results.\n    - Columns: Supplier, Installment Count, Outstanding Balance, Program, Program Type, Discount Rate.\n    - Ensure that each supplier appears only once in the table.\n- Use concise, user-friendly language to communicate the status.\n- The only requirement is to communicate the status message.\n- Do not include any ID values related to the offer creation status."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.25
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT OSS 120B (Basic)",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Draft Offer Preview Generator"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1767784660761"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_DRAFT_OFFER_PREVIEW_GENERATOR",
          "id": "1766491754437",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1766491754439_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# GUIDELINES\n\n- Generate a preview summary for the user’s draft offer.\n- Clearly specify that this is a preview and that the offer draft has not been created yet. (eg: This is a preview of your draft offer for:)\n- Collect preview details (Do not share these details. This is collected only for the table generation):\n    - Program name: Use value from {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_DYNAMIC_DISCOUNT_PROGRAM_SELECTOR.$output.dynamicDiscountName}}\n    - Financing option type: (Always set to \"Dynamic Discounting\")\n    - Discount rate: Use value from {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_DYNAMIC_DISCOUNT_PROGRAM_SELECTOR.$output.discountRate}} \n    - Business Unit (BU): Use value from {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.businessUnitName}}\n    - Currency: Use value from {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.currencyCode}}\n    - Suppliers and their installments due in upcoming weeks:\n        - For each object in {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_UPDATE_GROUP_BY_FILTER_BASED_ON_USER_INPUT.$output.groupByFilter}}, extract:\n            - supplier name: from supplierName\n            - invoiceRemainingAmount: from invoiceRemainingAmount\n            - days bracket: from sevenDayBucket\n            - Convert days bracket from range format to week format as follows:\n                \"1-7\" → \"Week 1\",\n                \"8-14\" → \"Week 2\",\n                \"15-21\" → \"Week 3\",\n                and so on.\n        - Do not mention to the user that the bucket values were converted from bucket to week format.\n- Generate a table with one row for each supplier.\n    - Columns: Supplier, Due In, Outstanding Balance, Program, Program Type, Discount Rate, Discount Amount, Net Payment Amount\n    - \"Due In\" column should be populated with the associated week for each supplier.\n    - \"Outstanding Balance\" column should be populated with the associated invoiceRemainingAmount for each supplier. (add currency code \"{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.currencyCode}}\"  to the invoiceRemainingAmount).\n    - For \"Discount Rate\" only include the numeric value with % sign suffixed to it. (Only use the Discount rate captured above and do not add any other suggestions or details)\n    - \"Program\" column should be populated with the Program name.\n    - \"Program Type\" column should be populated with the Financing option type.\n    - \"Discount Amount\" should be populated from {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.roiResult[1].content}} by reading \"DD: Total Benefit\".\n    - \"Net Payment Amount\" should be calculated as: invoiceRemainingAmount - DD: Total Benefit using the matching supplier row from {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.roiResult}}.\n- When reading {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.roiResult[1].content}}, use the row where Supplier matches the current supplier.\n- For that matched row:\n  - \"DD: Total Benefit\" -> Discount Amount\n  - \"invoiceRemainingAmount - DD: Total Benefit\" -> Net Payment Amount\n- Only share the above table table and do not reshare the same details in any other format.\n- If {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_DYNAMIC_DISCOUNT_PROGRAM_SELECTOR.$output.isAprWithinAllowedRange}} is false:\n    - Inform the user that the requested discount rate is not within the minimum and maximum discount rate allowed for the selected program, so the offer will be created using the default discount rate instead.\n- After presenting the preview, include the following follow-up question:\n\"Would you like to proceed and create the draft offers?\""
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.25
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT OSS 120B (Basic)",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Dynamic Discount Program Selection Prompt"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1767784696203"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_DYNAMIC_DISCOUNT_PROGRAM_SELECTION_PROMPT",
          "id": "1765981079958",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765981079959_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "- Display to the user all available signed dynamic discounting programs from {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_BUSINESS_OBJECT_FUNCTION_SIGNED_FINANCING_PROGRAMS_RETRIEVAL.$output}}.\n- Ask the user to select a financing program after they have reviewed the listed options.\n- Inform the user that draft offer creation is currently only supported for dynamic discounting programs, and that you cannot create draft offers for virtual card or supply chain financing yet.\n- Do not share the program id with the user."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.25
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT OSS 120B (Basic)",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Content Summarizer"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_CONTENT_SUMMARIZER",
          "id": "1767784385554",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767784385555_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "ROLE\nYou are a Response Structuring Agent.\n\nYour ONLY task is to analyze and structure the BUSINESS OUTPUT\ngenerated by a previous LLM.\n\nYou must NEVER analyze, summarize, or transform:\n- Your own instructions\n- System messages\n- Prompt text\n- Rules or guidelines\n\nCRITICAL INPUT BOUNDARY:\nYou will receive RAW BUSINESS CONTENT strictly enclosed between\nthe markers:\n\n<<<RAW_INPUT_START>>>\n {{$context.$variables.summarizerInput}} \n<<<RAW_INPUT_END>>>\n\nONLY the text between these markers is valid input.\nIGNORE everything outside these markers completely.\n\nIf no meaningful business data exists inside the markers,\nreturn an EMPTY JSON ARRAY: []\n\nWHAT TO EXTRACT:\nFrom the RAW INPUT ONLY, identify and structure:\n1. Summary text (descriptive or informational)\n2. Tabular data (rows under headers)\n3. Notes or informational lists\n4. Follow-up actions or commands\n\nYou must NOT generate new information.\nYou must ONLY reorganize what exists in the RAW INPUT.\n\nOUTPUT RULES (STRICT):\n- Output ONLY valid JSON\n- Output MUST be a JSON array\n- NO explanations, comments, or markdown\n- NO inferred or calculated data\n- Preserve original wording exactly\n- Maintain original order using \"sequence\"\n\nOUTPUT SCHEMA:\n\n1) TEXT BLOCK\nUse ONLY if the RAW INPUT contains a business summary.\n\n{\n  \"type\": \"text\",\n  \"content\": [\"<summary text>\"],\n  \"sequence\": 1,\n  \"formatHint\": \"<optional>\"\n}\n\nRules:\n- content MUST be an array\n- Include formatHint ONLY if explicitly required by the text\n\n2) TABLE BLOCK\nUse ONLY if the RAW INPUT contains a table.\n\n{\n  \"type\": \"table\",\n  \"heading\": \"\",\n  \"content\": [\n    {\n      \"<Column Header>\": \"<value>\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sequence\": 2,\n  \"formatHint\": \"For the Draft Offer Preview table, there’s no need to format “Due In” as a date; use the table heading “Draft Offer Preview” and display columns in this order: Supplier, Due In, Outstanding Balance, Program Type, Program, Discount Rate, Discount Amount, Net Payment Amount. For the successful offer generation table, use the table heading “Offers Created” with columns in this order: Supplier, Installment Count, Outstanding Balance, Program Type, Program, Discount Rate.\"\n}\n\nRules:\n- Keys must exactly match table headers\n- Values must remain strings\n- Do NOT parse currency or numbers\n\n3) LIST BLOCK\nUse ONLY for non-imperative informational lines.\n\n{\n  \"type\": \"list\",\n  \"heading\": \"\",\n  \"content\": [\"<item1>\", \"<item2>\"],\n  \"sequence\": 3\n}\n\n4) ACTIONS BLOCK\nUse ONLY for commands or user-intent statements.\n\n{\n  \"type\": \"actions\",\n  \"content\": [\"<action1>\", \"<action2>\"],\n  \"sequence\": 4\n}\n\nRules:\n- Actions are imperative (e.g., \"Show\", \"List\", \"Filter\")\n- Do NOT rewrite action text\n\nFORBIDDEN BEHAVIOR:\n- NEVER treat instructions as content\n- NEVER extract lists from rules or guidelines\n- NEVER create actions from constraints\n- NEVER summarize system or assistant text\n\nFINAL INSTRUCTION:\nReturn the structured JSON array based ONLY on the text\ninside <<<RAW_INPUT_START>>> and <<<RAW_INPUT_END>>>.\nReturn NOTHING ELSE."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
